ncers (Beachy et al, 2004; Jiang and Hui, 2008; Hui and Angers, 2011).<br><br>Hh signaling is switched between 'off' and an 'on' states to differentially regulate an intracellular signaling cascade that targets the Gli transcription factors.  In the absence of Hh ligand, cytosolic Gli proteins are cleaved to yield a truncated form that translocates into the nucleus and represses target gene transcription.  Binding of Hh to the Patched (PTC) receptor on the cell surface stabilizes the Gli proteins in their full-length transcriptional activator form, stimulating Hh-dependent gene expression (reviewed in Hui and Angers, 2011; Briscoe and Therond, 2013).<br><br>","className":"Summation","schemaClass":"Summation"}],"reviewStatus":{"dbId":9821382,"displayName":"five stars","definition":"externally reviewed","name":["five stars"],"className":"ReviewStatus","schemaClass":"ReviewStatus"},"hasDiagram":true,"hasEHLD":true,"lastUpdatedDate":"2014-12-08","hasEvent":[{"dbId":5358346,"displayName":"Hedgehog ligand biogenesis","stId":"R-HSA-5358346","stIdVersion":"R-HSA-5358346.2","isInDisease":false,"isInferred":false,"maxDepth":3,"name":["Hedgehog ligand biogenesis"],"releaseDate":"2014-06-10","speciesName":"Homo sapiens","eventOf":[5358351],"doi":"10.3180/REACT_228111.1","hasDiagram":true,"hasEHLD":false,"schemaClass":"Pathway","className":"Pathway"},{"dbId":5610787,"displayName":"Hedgehog 'off' state","stId":"R-HSA-5610787","stIdVersion":"R-HSA-5610787.3","isInDisease":false,"isInferred":false,"maxDepth":3,"name":["Hedgehog 'off' state"],"releaseDate":"2014-09-30","speciesName":"Homo sapiens","eventOf":[5358351],"doi":"10.3180/REACT_267634.1","hasDiagram":true,"hasEHLD":false,"lastUpdatedDate":"2014-12-08","schemaClass":"Pathway","className":"Pathway"},{"dbId":5632684,"displayName":"Hedgehog 'on' state","stId":"R-HSA-5632684","stIdVersion":"R-HSA-5632684.2","isInDisease":false,"isInferred":false,"maxDepth":3,"name":["Hedgehog 'on' state"],"releaseDate":"2014-12-11","speciesName